+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` walks trades within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`) starting from the most recently closed trade, backwards, counting an unbroken streak of losing trades (`close_profit` below `required_profit`, which defaults to `0.0`).
+Once that streak reaches `trade_limit` trades in a row, trading stops for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`).
+
+Unlike `StoplossGuard`, this is based purely on consecutive losses, not on total or windowed profit, and any exit reason counts - a single winning (or breakeven) trade resets the streak.
+
+This applies across all pairs, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, which will then only look at one pair at a time.
+
+Similarly, this protection will by default look at all trades (long and short). For futures bots, setting `only_per_side` will make the bot only consider one side, and will then only lock this one side.
+
+The below example stops trading for all pairs for 12 candles after 4 losing trades occurred in a row within the last 48 candles.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 48,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+            "only_per_side": False
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
